"The six lane reports were **not present in my input** — so I re-derived the chain from the images myself. Everything below is graded against what I actually read this session.\n\n---\n\n# FK‑22 · The actor‑pool gate — settled end to end (offline)\n\n**Method:** read‑only static analysis. Images: `dumps/s129-poolgate/SUPERVIVE-Win64-Shipping.dump.exe` (ImageBase `0x7FF7B86D0000`), cross‑checks in `tools/extractor/out` (already‑extracted shipped assets). Zero launches, zero injection, zero writes.\n\n⚠ **Provenance note.** This document does **not** synthesize six lane reports — none reached me. It is a single‑analyst derivation. Where a prior lane may have claimed something I did not measure, I say *not established* rather than repeating it.\n\n---\n\n## 1. THE GATE, END TO END\n\n`ULokiActorPoolManager` vtable is `.rdata 0x08877A80`; `0x08877A80 + 0x2D0 = 0x08877D50`, i.e. **displacement `0x2D0` = slot 90** [M], and `findptr 0x56363F0` returns **exactly one** `.rdata` occurrence — `0x08877D50` — so the override is unfolded and lives in exactly one vtable [M]. Slot 90 (`0x56363F0`, 93 B, page `0x05636000` **present** [M]) does, in order: **(i)** `call 0x0B9E1F0` = `mov al,1; ret` — the engine base's slot 90 (`0x07DE3618 + 0x2D0 = 0x07DE38E8` holds bytes `f0 e1 26 b9 f7 7f 00 00` → RVA `0x0B9E1F0` [M]), so `Super::` is a constant `true` and can never be the FALSE source. ⚠ **`0x0B9E1F0` is folded 26,444×** (uncapped qword‑pointer count over the whole image [M]) — it is the universal `mov al,1; ret` stub and names nothing; the [M] claim is about the *engine vtable slot*, not the address. **(ii)** `call 0x12C7260` = the stock `UObject::GetWorld` forwarder (`mov rcx,[rcx+0x28]` = `Outer`; `jmp [vtable+0x188]`, `0x188/8 = 49`, and slot 49 of this same vtable *is* `0x12C7260` [M]) → a `UWorld*`. **(iii)** `lea rbx,[World+0x258]`, `cmp qword [rbx],0` — a non‑null object pointer. **(iv)** `call 0x5380690` = **`ALokiGameState::StaticClass()`**, confirmed two independent ways: `strxref func` shows its `GetPrivateStaticClassBody` literals `'ALokiGameState' / '/Script/Loki' / 'Game'`, and `vtables.py name ALokiGameState` independently reports `gpsc 0x5380690` [M]. **(v)** `call 0x12C7DD0` = an `IsA`: reads `obj->Class` at `+0x18` (this build's `classOff`) then walks `FStructBaseChain` (`[UClass+0x38]` array, `[UClass+0x40]` depth) [M]. **(vi)** `mov rax,[rbx]; movzx eax, byte [rax+0x898]; ret`.\n\n⇒ **`ULokiActorPoolManager::<slot 90>()` returns `((ALokiGameState*)GetWorld()->GameState)->bSupportsActorPoolPriming`, a plain `bool` at `ALokiGameState+0x898`** [M]. `World+0x258` = `UWorld::GameState` is [I‑strong] — inferred solely from the `IsA(ALokiGameState)` target, not from a UWorld layout oracle.\n\n**The byte at `+0x898` is named, measured, not inferred.** The ASCII UHT name `bSupportsActorPoolPriming` sits at `.rdata 0x08986178`; its `FBoolPropertyParams` record begins at `.rdata 0x08983A50` (`NameUTF8 → 0x08986178`, `RepNotifyFunc = 0`, `PropertyFlags = 0x0010040000010001`, `Flags = 0x4C`, `ObjectFlags = 0x45`, `Setter/GetterFunc = 0`, then `01 00 | 01 00 | 20 0b 00 00`) and its **`SetBitFunc` pointer is `0x53800D0`, whose entire body is `c6 81 98 08 00 00 01 / c3` = `mov byte ptr [rcx + 0x898], 1; ret`** [M]. Self‑validating: the trailing `0x0B20` field (= `sizeof(ALokiGameState)`, [I]) exceeds `0x898`, and `SetBitFunc` is a single‑occurrence pointer (1 qword image‑wide) [M]. A whole‑byte store means it is a real `bool`, not a bitfield.\n\n**Two more facts that invert the naive reading:**\n\n* **The C++ default is `true`.** `InternalConstructor<ALokiGameState>` (`0x5382ED0`, attributed to `ALokiGameState` by `vtables.py`) tail‑jumps `0x5382EDE → 0x5676AA0` [M], and a capstone sweep of `0x5676AA0..0x5676FCC` lands **exactly** on `0x5676F10 = mov byte ptr [rdi + 0x898], 1`, embedded in a strictly ascending member‑init run (`+0x7d0, 0x7d8, … 0x890, 0x898, 0x8a0, … 0x8d4`) — the unmistakable shape of a constructor initialiser list [M]. ⇒ **`ALokiGameState::ALokiGameState()` sets `bSupportsActorPoolPriming = true`.**\n* **The Tutorial Blueprint overrides it to `false`.** From the already‑extracted shipped assets, `tools/extractor/out/bpdump_BP_LokiGameState_Tutorial_PROPS.txt:52` reads verbatim:\n  `- bSupportsActorPoolPriming (BoolProperty) = False (BoolProperty)` [M].\n  Same line in `bpdump_BP_LokiGameState_PvE_Holdout_PROPS.txt:52`; `BP_LokiGameState_FFA.json` carries `\"bSupportsActorPoolPriming\": false` [M]. `BP_LokiGameState`, `BP_LokiGameStateRounds`, `BP_LokiGameState_Battlefield` **do not serialize the key at all** (their PROPS dumps are populated — 136 / 69 lines, 2 `BoolProperty` each — so this is a real absence, not an empty dump) ⇒ they inherit `true` [M + I]. ★ A BP CDO serializes *deltas against its archetype*, so the mere **presence** of the override independently corroborates that the native default is `true`.\n  S124 measured the live tutorial GameState as `BP_LokiGameState_Tutorial_C` (CLAUDE.md) — **the exact class that ships `False`.**\n\n**And the priming caller is on the same object.** `callxref 0x3356000` (`UActorPoolManager::PrimePools`) returns **exactly one** call site: `0x0567AA50` [M], inside the function `0x567A1B0..0x567B0FF` which carries the ASCII literal **`'ALokiGameState::BeginPlay'`** (+0xAB1) and `'Entering game state %s'` [M]. `findptr 0x567A1B0` = 1 occurrence, a vtable slot [M]. ⇒ **`ALokiGameState::BeginPlay()` → `PrimePools()` → slot 90 → its own `bSupportsActorPoolPriming`** — the gate, the reader, the caller and the override are all one object.\n\n---\n\n## 2. THE REPAIR CLASS — ranked by cost\n\n| # | Class | Verdict | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **(b) DATA poke on the live object** — one byte `GameState+0x898 = 1` | **The mechanism**, but *insufficient alone* | The gate reads exactly one byte on one object [M]. Project hazard ladder puts a data poke at the safest tier (nothing 0/22 · bytecode 0/9 vs standing `.text` 7/8). Readback is free (`movzx` the same byte). |\n| 2 | **(c) requires calling `PrimePools`** | **Also required** | `PrimePools` has **one** caller — `ALokiGameState::BeginPlay` [M] — which has already run and taken the skip branch by the time any shim is injected. Poking the byte afterwards changes nothing retroactively. `PrimePools` is **not reflected** (`strxref native \"PrimePools\"` → *no ASCII reflection name*) [M], so the S55 UFunction primitive cannot reach it by name; it needs a **plain direct call** to `0x3356000` with `rcx` = the manager — same call class as the settled FK‑27 `AddToRoot` recipe, no `.text` write. It self‑heals its own preconditions (`'…PoolableActorClasses were not generated ahead of time, looking for them now…'`) and is re‑entrancy‑guarded (`'…Called while priming is already in progress.'`) [M, both literals in its body]. |\n| 3 | **(a) ini / config, no injection** | **NO** | `PropertyFlags = 0x0010040000010001` [M]; `& 0x4000 == 0` and `& 0x20 == 0`. Mapping those bits to `CPF_Config` / `CPF_Net` is [I], but the raw bits are [M]: this property carries no config or replication bit. The value that actually loses is a **Blueprint CDO delta baked into the pak**, and loose‑file/AR‑bin deployment is already recorded INERT in this IoStore build. |\n| 4 | **(d) not the actual blocker** | **Cannot be excluded** — see §3 | The gate explains why the *pool is empty*. It does **not** by itself explain a NULL from the spawn path, because the spawn path never reads the gate (§3). If priming succeeds and the pooled spawn still returns NULL, the gate was a real but non‑terminal blocker. |\n\n**Manager handle, free:** `AGameStateBase::GetActorPoolManager`‑shaped accessor `0x3840490` opens with `mov rax,[rcx+0x428]; test rax,rax; jne <return it>` and validates `[rcx+0x430]` against `UActorPoolManager::GetPrivateStaticClass` (`0x32A8570`, independently named by `vtables.py`) [M]. ⇒ **`GameState+0x428` = the cached `UActorPoolManager*`, `GameState+0x430` = its class.** One RPM read gets the manager; no call needed.\n\n---\n\n## 3. THE §2 ANSWER — the spawn path wants a **primed pool**, not the gate\n\n`SpawnPoolableActorFromClass` and `…Deferred` are UFUNCTIONs on **`ULokiBlueprintLibrary`** (`FClassFunctionLinkInfo` table `0x08978D98`, 159 entries) [M]. Exec thunk `0x537EEE0` → **impl `0x566FF50`** (`callers=1`) [M]. That impl: class non‑null → `IsA(AActor)` (`0x338BD10` = `AActor::StaticClass()`, string‑confirmed) → `GetWorldFromContextObject` → **the identical `World+0x258` / `ALokiGameState::StaticClass()` / `IsA` sequence at `0x566FFFA–0x5670018`** → `call 0x3840490` (fetch manager) → `call 0x5647F00` → `0x5648050` (the worker) [M].\n\nThe worker's operative step is `0x56482C2–0x56482E5`: a **murmur3 finaliser** (`imul 0x85ebca6b`, `imul 0xc2b2ae35`) over the class hash, then `lea rcx,[rsi+0x38]; call 0x334E7A0` — a `TMap` lookup on **`ActorPoolManager+0x38`**, followed by a loop that walks the returned `TArray`, skips entries whose `ObjectFlags` (`obj+0x0C`, this build's layout) have bit 30 set, and `memmove`s dead slots out [M]. That is *take an actor out of the pool for this class*.\n\n**An exhaustive `.text` scan for `FF 9x D0 02 00 00` (`call qword ptr [reg+0x2D0]`) finds 524 sites image‑wide; filtered to the two pooling code ranges there are exactly 3 engine sites (`0x331FD07`, `0x33427E1`, `0x33560C5`) and 3 Loki‑pool sites (`0x56400E1`, `0x5644325`, `0x564438D`) — and NONE of them falls inside `0x566FF50..0x5670070` or `0x5648050..0x5648F00`** [M]. Both pages are decrypted in the s129 image [M]. ⇒ **the pooled‑spawn path never re‑consults slot 90.** (Caveat: the scan sees only *direct* `call [reg+disp]`; a `mov rax,[rax+0x2D0]; call rax` split would be missed — [I] that MSVC does not emit that here.)\n\n⇒ **Repair implied: (b) AND (c), in that order and in one arming window.** Poke `GameState+0x898 = 1`, then directly call `PrimePools(GameState+0x428)`. The byte alone is inert on the spawn path; the call alone re‑hits the skip branch.\n\n---\n\n## 4. THE BYPASS — hand‑spawning the pod\n\n**Viable to the point of having a pod actor, then it dies at FK‑1's wall.** The context establishes [M, prior] that `BP_DropPod_C` spawns fine through the ordinary path, and CLAUDE.md records [M] that `Default__BP_DropPlane_Base_C` sets `TeamDropPodClass = BP_DropPod_C`, that `SpawnDropPodForTeam` has no marker query and only two bail points, and that `InitializeDropPod` touches `DropShip` only under `bIsTeamLeaderPod`. So a hand‑spawned pod is reachable without the pool at all.\n\n**It terminates at the pod→hero handoff.** `ALokiDropPod::AuthBeginGlideDiveFromDropPod` and `ALokiDropPlane::AddPlayerToPlane` are **empty impls folding to `0x0F7EC20` (`ret 0`)** — and that address is folded **165,789×** image‑wide [M, uncapped scan], so it identifies nothing and must never be named after one caller. `ALokiGameMode::SpawnPlayer` folds to `0x0F7EB50` (`xor eax,eax; ret`, **27,217×** [M]). Those are FK‑1's four stripped server‑authority functions, untouched by anything here.\n\n⇒ The bypass buys you **a pod in the world and no rider**. It is worth doing only as a *diagnostic* — it separates \"the pool is the blocker\" from \"the pool is one of several blockers\" — not as a route to a playable drop.\n\n---\n\n## 5. PRE‑REGISTERED EXPERIMENT (written before it runs)\n\n**Cheapest next flight. Runs inside one already‑staged tutorial world (S124 recipe), no relaunch between arms.**\n\n**Phase A — read‑only RPM, zero risk, run first.** Read, in this order: `World+0x258`; that object's UClass name; `byte [GS+0x898]`; `qword [GS+0x428]`; `[mgr+0x38]` TMap element count.\n*Pre‑registered prediction:* class = `BP_LokiGameState_Tutorial_C`; `[GS+0x898] == 0`; `[GS+0x428] != 0`; pool map count `== 0`.\n**★ Phase A alone can falsify the entire model at zero cost:** if `[GS+0x898]` already reads **1**, the FALSE must come from the null‑check or the `IsA` leg, and §1's BP‑override story is wrong. Do not proceed to Phase B in that case.\n\n**Phase B — the flight. Single variable: one byte.** Arm order **A → B → A**.\n* **Arm A (control):** direct call `PrimePools(mgr)` at `0x3356000`, `rcx = *(GS+0x428)`. Nothing else.\n* **Arm B (treatment):** write `byte [GS+0x898] = 1`, **readback‑verify it reads 1**, then the *identical* `PrimePools(mgr)` call.\n* Nothing else differs — same process, same manager pointer, same call site, same arming mechanism.\n\n**Arming class:** heap `UFunction.Func` swap (`RM_PHASELADDER` pattern, `KFSNAME=\"\"` if at menu‑ish dispatch). **Never `RM_GOTOPHASE` / `InstallHook()`** — that is the standing `ProcessInternal` `.text` patch measured at 10/10 vs 3/36.\n\n**Positive control — free and built in.** `PrimePools` logs before it decides: a reachable call **cannot** be silent. Arm A must produce **exactly one new** `UActorPoolManager::PrimePools : Feature is not enabled, skipping.` line. ⚠ Baseline‑count first: that string is already in the log from `BeginPlay`, so **presence does not discriminate — only the count does.** A silent arm ⇒ the call never landed ⇒ **the sitting is VOID and nothing else may be interpreted.**\n\n**Confound being killed:** \"the pool is empty\" currently has three indistinguishable causes — priming never ran / priming ran and matched nothing / the byte at `+0x898` is not what slot 90 reads. Arm A vs Arm B differ in exactly one byte, so a divergence attributes to the byte and nothing else.\n\n**PASS readout (Arm B):** the `Feature is not enabled, skipping.` count does **not** increase; instead one or both of `%d actor classes found for priming.` / `%d actor classes passed filtering for this match and will be loaded.` appear with `%d > 0`; and after ≥5 s (the second string says *will be loaded* — treat priming as async) `[mgr+0x38]` element count is **> 0**.\n**FAIL readout (Arm B):** the skip line count increments again **with `byte [GS+0x898]` reading 1 on readback**.\n\n**What FALSIFIES the whole model:**\n1. Phase A finds `[GS+0x898] == 1` already → the gate's FALSE comes from the null/`IsA` legs, not the CDO.\n2. Arm B: verified `1` at `+0x898` and the skip line still fires → `World+0x258` is not the object slot 90 reads, or `IsA(ALokiGameState)` fails, or `+0x898` is not the read field. All three are checkable in the same RPM pass.\n3. **Phase C (cheap, same window):** with the pool primed, call `SpawnPoolableActorFromClass(BP_DropPod_C)`. If it *still* returns NULL, then §2's repair class **(d)** is the truth — the pool gate was real but not terminal — and the next blocker is downstream of `0x5648050`.\n\n---\n\n## 6. OPEN QUESTIONS + INSTRUMENT ARTIFACTS\n\n### Open (not established — do not invent an answer)\n1. **Which leg of the gate actually fails live.** The BP CDO `False` is [M] *in the asset*; that it is what the live object carries is [I]. Phase A settles it in one read.\n2. **Does the pooled worker fall back to a fresh spawn on a pool miss?** Its late region (`0x5648CEE..0x5649200`) calls `0x339B7A0` (697 B, no literals, unnamed), `0x3392820`, `0x339D420`, `0x39C3DB0`, `0x3F49C20`. `0x339B7A0` is *plausibly* `UWorld::SpawnActor` — **[S], not read.** Until this is graded, \"empty pool ⇒ NULL\" is [I] resting on the empirical NULL, not on the code.\n3. **Two other engine consumers of vtable slot 0x2D0** — `0x331FD07` (in fn `0x331FC80`, 238 B) and `0x33427E1` (in fn `0x33427C0`, 47 B). `callxref` finds **zero direct E8 callers** for either, so both their identity and their reachability are unknown.\n4. **Whether `BP_DropPod_Tutorial_C` survives PrimePools' own filter** (`'%d actor classes passed filtering for this match…'`). The startup `LogActorPooling` registrations suggest yes; unverified.\n5. **`World+0x258` = `UWorld::GameState`** — [I‑strong], from the `IsA` target only. No UWorld layout oracle was consulted.\n6. **`sizeof(ALokiGameState) = 0xB20`** — [I], read as the `SizeOfOuter` field of a `FBoolPropertyParams` whose exact 5.4 layout I did not independently verify. The bytes are [M].\n\n### Instrument artifacts caught this session\n1. **`fkdis.py findptr` caps its output at 200 rows.** I first read \"200\" as the fold multiplicity of `0x0B9E1F0`; an uncapped scan gives **26,444**. ⇒ *a row count from `findptr` is a floor, never a count.* This is the exact shape that produces a bogus \"this stub is used in 200 places\" claim.\n2. **`fkdis.py d <rva>` returns a blank result when `<rva>` is not an instruction boundary** (`0x56481D0` → one empty line; `0x56481D7` → 109 instructions). A blank disassembly reads exactly like \"page not decrypted\" and is not.\n3. **`strxref.py func` extents are per‑`.pdata` ROW, not per function.** `SpawnPoolableActorFromClass` reports \"59 bytes\" and is far larger; the `.pdata` chaining that S124 hit on `GoToPhase` is systemic. **Never take a function size from that line.**\n4. **The tool told me its own entry was wrong and I nearly ignored it.** `func 0x5676F10` printed `entry 0x5676AC3 [.pdata EXACT] (heuristic said 0x5676AA0 -- missed the entry)`. Sweeping from `0x5676AC3` desynced the whole constructor; the *heuristic* value `0x5676AA0` was correct, and `callxref` confirmed it as a `jmp` target. **Read the caveat line, not just the number.**\n5. **Naming a folded stub after one caller.** `0x0B9E1F0` (26,444×), `0x0F7EC20` (165,789×), `0x0F7EB50` (27,217×) — all measured uncapped this session. \"The base `IsFeatureEnabled` returns true\" is a statement about **engine vtable slot 90 of `0x07DE3618`**, not about the address.\n6. **Offset `0x898` identifies nothing on its own.** Six `mov byte [reg+0x898], 1` sites exist image‑wide (`0x01438825`, `0x023469AF`, `0x031D830F`, `0x03C995E1`, `0x053800D0`, `0x05676F10`) [M]; four belong to unrelated classes. The link to `bSupportsActorPoolPriming` is the **UHT `SetBitFunc` pointer**, and only that.\n7. **My own capstone sweep printed negative RVAs** because I subtracted `ImageBase` from values that were already RVAs (these dumps are flat: file offset == RVA). Caught only because the sign was absurd — a smaller offset error would have decoded plausibly and been written up.\n8. **A missing key in a `bpdump …_PROPS.txt` is only interpretable after you check the dump is populated.** `BP_LokiGameState_PROPS.txt` lacks the key *and* has 136 lines / 2 `BoolProperty` entries — so the absence is a real inherit‑the‑default, not an empty file. Absence in an unchecked dump would have been uninterpretable."